# ZKTeco Attendance Bridge — Server Migration & Troubleshooting Notes

**Stack:** Django + Gunicorn (Unix socket) + Celery/Redis + PostgreSQL + Nginx, `pyzk` for ZKTeco F18 device communication
**OS:** Ubuntu 26.04 LTS
**Scope:** Migration of the attendance bridge to a new on-prem server, debugging of sync failures, and dual-IP network failover setup.

> All IPs, MAC addresses, hostnames, credentials, and identifiers below are placeholders.

---

## 1. Environment Overview

| Component | Detail |
|---|---|
| App server | `<SERVER_IP>` (on-prem, Ubuntu 26.04) |
| Biometric device | ZKTeco F18 at `<DEVICE_IP>:4370` (UDP) |
| Database | PostgreSQL, bound to `127.0.0.1:5432` (local-only) |
| Task queue | Celery + Redis (`redis://localhost:6379/0`) |
| App root | `/var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge` |
| Services | `zk-bridge` (Gunicorn web), `zk-worker` (Celery worker), `zk-beat` (Celery beat) |

