## 2. Migration Steps

### 2.1 Database dump & restore

```bash
# On old server
pg_dump -U <DB_USER> -d <DB_NAME> -F c -b -v -f attendance_bridge_backup.dump

# Transfer
scp attendance_bridge_backup.dump <USER>@<SERVER_IP>:/tmp/

# On new server
pg_restore -U <DB_USER> -d <DB_NAME> -v /tmp/attendance_bridge_backup.dump
```

### 2.2 Codebase & environment

```bash
git clone <REPOSITORY_URL> /var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge
cd /var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge
# Create .env with DB credentials, CRM endpoint, device settings
```

Key `.env` values (DB is local-only, so the host must be loopback — not the LAN IP):

```
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=5432
CRM_API_URL=<CRM_DOMAIN>
```

### 2.3 Systemd service (final version)

`/etc/systemd/system/zk-bridge.service` — uses `RuntimeDirectory` so `/run/zk-bridge/` is created with correct permissions on start and cleaned up on stop:

```ini
[Unit]
Description=ZKTeco Attendance Bridge Web Server
After=network.target postgresql.service redis.service

[Service]
User=<SERVICE_USER>
Group=www-data
WorkingDirectory=/var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge
EnvironmentFile=/var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge/.env
RuntimeDirectory=zk-bridge
ExecStart=/var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge/.venv/bin/gunicorn \
    --workers 3 \
    --bind unix:/run/zk-bridge/zk-bridge.sock \
    --umask 007 \
    --timeout 300 \
    attendance_bridge.wsgi:application
Restart=always

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

### 2.4 Nginx reverse proxy

`/etc/nginx/sites-available/zk-bridge` — listens on both server IPs, serves static/media directly, proxies the rest to the Gunicorn socket:

```nginx
server {
    listen 80;
    server_name <SERVER_IP> <SECONDARY_IP>;
    client_max_body_size 10M;

    location /static/ {
        alias /var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge/staticfiles/;
    }

    location /media/ {
        alias /var/www/systems/zkteco-f18-attendance-bridge/media/;
    }

    location / {
        include proxy_params;
        proxy_pass http://unix:/run/zk-bridge/zk-bridge.sock;
    }
}
```

Django must allow both hosts:

```python
ALLOWED_HOSTS = ['<SERVER_IP>', '<SECONDARY_IP>', 'localhost', '127.0.0.1']
```

Enable and apply:

```bash
sudo ln -s /etc/nginx/sites-available/zk-bridge /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl restart zk-bridge nginx
```

